CORE
reduction_partial.c
--evaluation-order-check
^Evaluation-order reduction: 1 of 2 side effects commute with all side effects they are unordered with$
^\[main\.evaluation-order\.\d+\] line 17 value of x is independent of evaluation order: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 18 g executes once: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
g neither accesses x nor what f accesses, so it is executed once. f writes x,
which is read as the first operand, so f is still executed in each of its
rounds, and the read of x is reported to depend on the evaluation order.
